WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.800
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.660
'Fort of Eggman Falls.' Mr. President...

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.000
You're guaranteed to win the next presidential election.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.660
I'm not so certain.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.130
In the battle against Eggman, the hero was Sonic.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.130
What? Sonic?

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.050
Sonic?

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:56.470
Sonic?

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.010
Sonic?

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.640
Sonic? Sonic? Sonic? Sonic?

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.940
Everything is about Sonic!

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.190
Sonic!

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.900
At this rate, Sonic will be elected president.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.530
Don't be ridiculous.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.040
I'm not kidding!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.830
Jerome, there's no need to be so serious.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.590
Trouble...

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.130
Alright, I have a plan!

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.970
Mr. President, you will host 'The Destruction of Eggman's Base Celebration Charity Party.'

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.220
The Destruction of Eggman's Base Celebration Charity Party?

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.310
We're going to invite Sonic to the party.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.190
We'll make Sonic shake hands with you, Mr. President.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:02.320
The next day, the TV shows and newspapers will be filled with stories about the President and Sonic.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:09.410
Your popularity will grow rapidly, and you will definitely be elected President in the next election.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:16.590
I'll send Sonic an invitation right now to attend The Destruction of Eggman's Base Celebration Charity Party.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.340
Hey...

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.740
Episode 14

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.740
Chase After the Hero Sonic!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.310
I'm going out for a bit.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.320
Sonic, there's a letter for you.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.410
What? The President?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.240
The Destruction of Eggman's Base Celebration Charity Party.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.040
An invitation card?

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:53.370
Of course the invitation is for Sonic, but we're invited too.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.210
Okay! Let's make new tuxedos and dresses, and we'll all go!

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.630
I'm sure there's going to be extravagant meals.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.100
Amy...

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.060
I'm home.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:13.980
Sonic!

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.400
It's incredible. You received a party invitation from the President.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:21.650
A party?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.700
We all get to go.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.740
You can go, right?

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.620
When is the party?

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:27.620
It's the day after tomorrow.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.200
I'll pass.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.330
What? Why?

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.330
I made a promise with Helen.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.960
Helen? You mean that Helen?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.130
Yeah. Your classmate, Chris.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.550
What do you mean?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.550
I ran into her the other day.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.780
Leave it to me!

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.240
Thank you. You're Sonic, aren't you?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.580
Do you know me?

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:12.500
I'm...

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.000
I know. You're Chris's classmate.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:15.710
Helen.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.920
I thought so.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.590
I came to look at that island. I always come to look at it.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:26.930
That island?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.470
Papa told me that there are many beautiful tiny white flowers growing on that island.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.270
Papa said that he'd take me there someday.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.690
But Papa is too busy.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.690
Adults like to be busy.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.860
But Papa is busy because of me.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:48.910
My...

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.870
Do you want to go to that island?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.000
I want to, but...

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.080
Would you like me to take you there?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.580
What?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.310
That's the story. Oops, I have to get going.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.110
Chuck, where's the boat and life jackets?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.440
Try looking in the storage room.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:47.340
Okay, all that's left is for the President to shake hands with Sonic. I'll make sure the press can take good pictures.

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.490
Where's Sonic? We've been waiting for you. He came? They're here!

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.580
He's not coming.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.620
This way!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.500
What's the point if Sonic's not coming? I'm going home.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.300
We have better things to do, you know.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.220
Please wait!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.310
I promise I'll bring Sonic.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.970
Please enjoy the food inside while you wait.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.730
Hey, you guys!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.520
Go to Sonic's house and bring him here!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.400
Yes sir!

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:58.120
We're from the government. We'd like to see Sonic.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.370
You didn't even knock and you order me to get Sonic?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.540
So you think you're big shots. Too bad, but he's not in.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.880
You shouldn't hide things from us.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:12.420
I have no reason to hide anything. You're bothering me, so leave.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.890
How dare you! Ignore her and search for Sonic!

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.970
Tanaka!

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.400
Are you intending to interfere?

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:28.190
Intefere? I'm merely getting rid of rude intruders.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.320
Excuse me.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.830
What? He's not at home?

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.370
It seems it will not work out as you planned.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.710
You're wrong! I'll make sure it works out as I planned!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.210
Connect me to army!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.670
Mr. Secretary, this is an emergency! Mobilize all the troops!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:57.010
If you don't have enough people, then get help from the Intelligence Department and the Office of Science and Technology!

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.680
Get Sonic!

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.350
Get him no matter what it takes!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.910
System all green. We have an image. We will start the search now.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.250
Our target is Sonic. He moves at 700 miles per hour, so stay alert.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.680
We have confirmation.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.390
Where?

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.060
In the S-13 district.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:43.770
He's at S-13 district.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:44.270
Roger.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.230
He is currently moving north at approximately 400 miles per hour.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.270
Don't you dare lose track of him!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:52.860
We've lost track of him.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:56.030
Find him no matter what it takes, you idiot!

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.370
It sure is noisy.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.910
Wait here. I'll go get the boat.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:12.340
Sonic isn't coming.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.050
Let's go home.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.420
Would you care for some champagne?

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:20.180
Hey, bring another round of hors d'oeuvres!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.810
Sheesh, what's taking the army so long?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.230
Signal confirmed.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:35.650
It's Sonic!

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.360
We found Sonic. He's at the Thorndyke residence.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:43.990
There he is!

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.040
Use the tear gas.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:47.910
Roger.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.810
We failed. Sonic is once again heading north.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.480
What's going on?

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.700
We're no match for him.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.740
Sonic went off the road? Which way? Towards the lake?

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.210
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.420
Let's go.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.130
Where's Sonic?

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.710
How long are you going to make us wait?

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:39.800
Please calm down.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:43.760
I've opened a 1969 Chateau Latour.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.350
Why don't you at least have one drink?

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.760
Here you go.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.310
Enjoy.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:49.810
One more glass.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.280
It's getting late.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:03.570
I'm getting excited. I wonder what kind of flowers there are.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.580
Even though I was supposed to come here with Papa...

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:12.460
I'm sure Papa is working really hard right now.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.630
Douglas, about your shift next week…

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.630
Do you want me to hire a part-time assistant for you? The way things are going...

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:26.390
It's fine. I'll also work the night shift.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.260
I see. Thanks.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.100
I need the work.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.150
We're almost there.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.030
They've come again.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.080
What is it?

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.540
Stay away!

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.400
Drag them to the shore.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.110
Damn! Are you scared?

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:28.740
I'm fine.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.280
Okay!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.580
Hang on tight.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.520
We were a little short.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.990
Did I scare you?

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.250
This is great! This is so much fun! I've never been this thrilled in my life!

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.840
This is my first adventure ever!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.590
It's true that this is turning into an adventure.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.340
Helen, do you want more adventure?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.350
Of course!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.800
All right!

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.310
The target fled into the forest.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.560
Good. They're trapped like a rat.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.770
Send in the special forces.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:42.520
Roger.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.650
Hey, it's empty.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.320
Here's a refill.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.290
I wonder how Sonic is doing.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:16.010
Mama and Papa work really hard so that I can have everything I need.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.140
They buy me everything.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:24.310
They take me to the best doctors, and this wheelchair is also very expensive.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.940
But actually, I don't need anything.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.650
I would rather have Mama and Papa spend time with me.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:36.330
But I had fun today! This is the first time I felt so excited!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.620
It seems our adventure isn't over yet.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.800
I've spotted enemies behind us.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:48.960
Here we go.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:49.840
Okay.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.630
We've spotted Sonic! In pursuit!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.010
They're closing in.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.970
Just watch. I'll show you what adventure is really about!

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.570
That was easy.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.570
Sonic, up ahead!

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.120
Whoa!

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.420
They're coming.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.640
They're here.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.810
No problem!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:53.530
Climbing a cliff? That's not fair...

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:18.760
These are the tiny white flowers that Papa told me about.

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:27.650
Shall I pick some for you?

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.070
Don't!

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:35.530
I want to leave them as they are. I'd like to show this to Papa and Mama one day.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:38.950
I understand. Until then, it's a secret between the two of us.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.340
They sure are persistent.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.800
If they come here, they'll step on the flowers.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.220
Leave it to me.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.140
Hey!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.180
Over here!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.600
Over there!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.730
I'll shake them off fast.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.030
It's the ocean.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.200
Sonic!

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.590
Don't resist and come with us to the President's office.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:39.840
We won't be rough.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.600
I still have things to do.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.180
Then we have no choice.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.500
Do you know how to fly a helicopter?

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.370
I usually let Tails handle these things.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:11.460
Is this the one?

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.880
Don't leave anything behind.

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:30.640
Look, Sonic!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.620
The adventure is over.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.040
I guess so. Did you have fun?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.670
Yeah, lots!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.960
It's late. I'll take you home.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.880
Don't you have to see the President?

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.260
Forget about that.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:05.890
But I feel bad if you keep him waiting because of me.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:08.600
I'd like you to see him, even if it's for a short while.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.430
As you wish.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:17.440
What? You let him escape? You idiot! Where is he now?

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:18.860
What is it?

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:22.860
Sonic!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.160
Sonic, thank you very much for coming. Mr. President!

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.280
Mr. President!

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.750
Welcome, Sonic.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.210
Yes! This is the moment!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:40.420
Cameras! Cameras! Reporters! Reporters!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.510
What happened to the press?

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:05.240
Then they tried to capture us by firing a rope with a hook from a helicopter!

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:10.120
They first came at us from the left, like this.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:13.370
We tried to dodge to the right, but we were on a boat.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:17.330
We couldn't move fast enough, so we were hit right in the middle!

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:25.180
But we didn't panic. We quickly removed the hook, pulled up and used our opponent's actions as an advantage to...

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.840
Mama, I want a second helping!

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.550
All right. You sure have an appetite today.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.560
And then...

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.600
Wait! I'm going to have a second serving too.

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:37.150
I have to be fully prepared to listen to your story today.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:41.190
Hurry back, Papa. The best is yet to come!

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:45.530
The real adventure starts when we jump off the cliff.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:49.780
Okay, okay. Her story is going to last for about two bottles of wine.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:53.830
What's the matter?

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:58.460
She asked for seconds. She's so energetic.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.250
Mama...

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:03.050
We always kept her in the house because we thought it was too dangerous.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:07.340
I'll rethink my job schedule.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:09.680
Actually, I'll make sure it's changed.

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:13.560
I forgot that there was a place I wanted to take her.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:14.680
Papa...

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:17.270
Mama, Papa, what's taking so long?

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:18.940
We'll be right there.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:23.440
Hold your horses. My stew is special, so it takes time.

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:25.820
The story's just starting.

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:28.740
Guess what the enemy brought out after the helicopters?

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:32.160
Sky-flying motor bikes! Like the ones in the movies!

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:33.830
The ones that fly right above the ground.

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:36.450
Oh, and I also met the President.

00:22:36.620 --> 00:22:38.670
You don't have to rush. Take your time.

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:40.790
Remind me what happened after the helicopter pulled you up.

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:43.130
I don't know where to start anymore!

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:03.810 --> 00:24:05.810
<i></i>

00:24:30.170 --> 00:25:35.360
Raid of Egg Fort, the Flying Fortress!
